{
  "created": "2026-11-13",
  "purpose": "Research 09 P1-P6 and release prep R0.1-R0.4/R0.6: Windows run on the tree of c4c35a8 (worker deferral) with the probe fixes of b66f132; Linux run (scripts/linux/run.sh) on fbc54ba plus the working tree of a7f1523 (release prep + probe fixes). Product code of both runs is identical (c4c35a8).",
  "windows": "Windows 11 x64 MSVC release with static CRT, ConPTY via pywinpty, 12 logical CPUs; pty_clipboard.py used the real clipboard and restored its previous text.",
  "linux": "Debian 12 container under Docker Desktop 29.9.3 (WSL2 kernel), rustc 1.98.1, Python pty + pyte, private Xvfb clipboard; static musl binaries also run on debian:11, ubuntu:22.04, alpine:3.20, debian:12.",
  "notes": [
    "An earlier Windows run flagged one sample: answering the 12 MiB large-file prompt on one pinned CPU took 53.7 ms (terminal_write 52.3 ms) because the open worker started before the frame write; fixed in c4c35a8 (three reruns peak 15.6 ms; this run has no investigation).",
    "pty_agent.py hung 22 minutes on Windows in that run (unlocked second PTY reader); fixed in b66f132, 3/3 passes before this run.",
    "Not covered: macOS (not a release target), ARM, real Linux terminal emulators, Wayland clipboard, SSH/tmux."
  ],
